            <ArticleTitle>Obesity and Testosterone Levels in Ghanaian Men With Type 2 Diabetes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>61-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2337/diaclin.32.2.61</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Testosterone plays a vital role in obesity, glucose homeostasis, and lipid metabolism. The aim of this study was to investigate androgen levels and its association with obesity in Ghanaian men with type 2 diabetes. The study showed that serum total and free testosterone concentrations were lower in male patients with type 2 diabetes and that obesity was strongly associated with low levels of total and free testosterone in Ghanaian men with type 2 diabetes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
